# Step 13a: the core, in cortex-core, and what it added to cortex-base,
# cortex-tools, cortex-session and cortex-policy.
#
# Each seam between the core and the crate whose trait or hook it fills is
# broken here: an adapter that drops a case, trust not passed to one of the
# places that need it, a secret that reaches the disk, a variable left in a
# command's environment, an answer taken from a client that may not give it,
# a denial that does not stop. And each finding of the step's independent
# review, with the fix taken out.

[break] read-only-allow-told-as-allow
rule: A command the engine knows changes nothing is told to the loop as read-only, so it is scheduled beside other calls and not looked at for changes.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/policy.rs
find: Outcome::Allow { read_only: true } => Decision::AllowReadOnly
replace: Outcome::Allow { read_only: true } => Decision::Allow
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it gates::sys_a_command_that_only_reads_is_told_to_the_loop_as_changing_nothing

[break] denial-told-as-allow
rule: A call the engine denies is told to the loop as a denial, with the engine's reason.
file: crates/cortex-core/src/policy.rs
find:
    Outcome::Deny { reason } => Decision::Deny {
        reason: Some(reason),
    }
replace: Outcome::Deny { .. } => Decision::Allow
caught-by:
    cortex-core::it gates::a_rule_that_denies_is_a_refusal_with_its_reason_and_the_run_goes_on
    cortex-core::it settings::the_level_can_be_lowered_by_whoever_drives_and_raised_only_by_a_user

[break] write-not-shown-to-engine
rule: Every effect a call declares is shown to the engine: a write is judged as a write of its path.
