[break] engine-told-every-projects-rules-are-approved
rule: The engine sets a project's allow rules aside until its rules are the ones the user saw. Seen through the core, nothing changes when the engine is told otherwise: configuration has already held the project's rules back, so the engine is never given them. The engine's own tests hold its half (`cortex-policy`, an allow rule that needs trust is withheld).
